   "grade": "5.10a",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Sustained moderate climbing, mostly 5.8-5.9 with some cruxes at 5.9+ to 5.10-, ending on a summit with big views. P1 5.9 (180 ft): cracks over overhangs from the buttress's low point. P2 5.8 (190 ft): a corner and overhang, then 4th-5th class on the crest. P3 5.8 (140 ft): cracks and corners. P4 5.10- (180 ft): finger-crack corner, a bulge, an overhang. P5 5.10- (180 ft): cracks to a dark corner with a splitter. P6 5.9+ (130 ft): big corner, left over an overhang. P7 5.9: thin cracks, a chimney, the crest. P8 5.9 (200+ ft): simul or pitch out to a splitter at the summit.",
