   "name": "South Face",
   "grade": "5.4",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Cross blocks to ledges of Class 2 on the saddle's right-hand side. Beyond that, the South Ridge is a broad slope of talus and sand that steepens into Class 3 scrambling beneath the summit block. The crux is that block: a jam crack and a squeeze chimney lead to it, then use the crack along its eastern side to reach a lower neighboring block and step across, easy but bold, onto the top. Descend the route.",
