  "row": {
   "id": "ca_dragon_peak_north_arete",
   "area_id": "ca_dragon_peak",
   "name": "North Arete",
   "grade": "5.5 PG13",
   "discipline": "trad",
   "overview": "From the saddle between Dragon Peak and Dragons Tooth, head up the huge dihedral and crack system for two pitches rated 5.5 to 5.6. The system steepens into a chimney near its top and ends at a conspicuous gap in the ridge. Keep going up the exposed ridge to a second notch with a prominent tower, where one rappel and a 5.5 pitch get you across to the next tower. The rappel can reportedly be downclimbed at 5.8, but it is chossy and exposed. Staying right on the knife-edge crest all the way up, one last notch is crossed by an exposed downclimb on knobs before the top.",
   "description": null,
   "approach": "From the Onion Valley parking loop, take the trail that splits from the Kearsarge Pass trail and runs north into the basins holding Golden Trout Lake and the Dragon Peak lakes. Pass the waterfall on its right, cross the creek where the trail does, and climb to a meadow with large towers to the north. Camping is at the two lakes under the peak. At the last lake, aim for the chute on the climbers' right (north) side of the peak, not the south chute used by the scramble route. The climb starts in the big dihedral and chimney system reached from the col between Dragon Peak and Dragon's Tooth.",
